 "title": "Chase Excellence Not Money",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "The creator explains that instead of chasing money, you should chase excellence and mastery because money naturally follows excellence. By having intellectual curiosity to learn everything about your industry and mastering your craft, you build genuine value.",
 "key_points": [
  "Chase excellence and never chase money because money has an incredible way of finding excellence.",
  "Have the intellectual curiosity to learn everything you can about your industry and master it.",
  "Do not make money the destination; make mastery the destination.",
  "Money is a result of becoming exceptionally good at what you do, understanding your industry deeply, and solving valuable problems."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by By Founders. Text / caption: Stop chasing money. Chase excellence. Dr. George C. Fraser offers a fundamentally different way to think about success: don't make money the destination. Make mastery the destination. Money is a result. When you become exceptionally good at what you do, understand your industry deeply, solve valuable problems, and continuously improve your skills, financial opportunities become much more likely to follow. This is especially relevant for entrepreneurs. It's easy to become obsessed with revenue, valuation, followers, funding, or the next big opportunity. But those numbers can become distractions if you're not simultaneously building something genuinely valuable. The better question is: “How can I become so good at this that my work creates undeniable value?” That requires intellectual curiosity. Learn your industry. Study your customers. Understand the problems you're solving. Learn from competitors. Read. Experiment. Ask better questions. Develop expertise that compounds over time. Because excellence isn't created by occasionally working hard. It's created by becoming obsessed with getting better. The founders who build enduring companies aren't necessarily the people who chased money the hardest. They're often the people who became exceptionally good at understanding a problem and creating something people genuinely value. Focus on the craft. Master the industry. Build something excellent. And let money become a consequence of the value you create. Follow @byfounders_ for the stories, lessons, and mindsets behind extraordinary founders. Featured Icon: George C. Fraser #GeorgeCFraser #Motivation #Excellence #Inspiration #Success. Transcript: So let me say that differently. Chase excellence, and never chase money. Why? Because money has an incredible way of finding excellence. Did you chase excellence and not money? Do you have the intellectual curiosity to learn everything you can about this incredible industry and master it?",
